[[17592186060940 :tutorial/content "Suppose we are given a system of linear equations and its respective augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can apply some operations to the augmented matrix that do not change the set of solutions for the corresponding system. These operations are called **elementary row operations**. \n\nAfter applying an **elementary row operation** to the augmented matrix, the new corresponding system will have the same solutions.\n\nThere are three types of elementary row operations:\n\n- switching any two rows: \n\n$$\nR_i \\leftrightarrow R_j\n$$\n\n- multiplying (each element of) a row by a non-zero number: \n\n$$\nR_i := k R_i,\\qquad k \\neq 0\n$$\n\n- adding a multiple of one row to another row: \n\n$$\nR_j := R_j+k R_i,\\qquad j \\neq i\n$$\n\nIn the notations above, the \"$:=$\" symbol is called the **assignment operator.** We use this to assign new values to every element of a given row.\n\nFor example, the row operation $R_1 := 2 R_1$ means, \"create a new row $1$ by taking the old row $1$ and multiplying it by $2.$\" When we do this, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{1}:=2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 3 & 2\\cdot (-1) & 2\\cdot 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA few final points on notation.\n\n- We use the similarity symbol ($\\sim$) to indicate when one matrix is transformed into another matrix using elementary row operations.\n\n- The assignment operator $:=$ is sometimes called the \"walrus operator\" because it looks like a walrus on its side!"] [17592186059580 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n![](images/62/627d12115d61ddfdedf9db08330269de2137a23abceada977d039e90e5b88675.png)\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_2 := R_2 +(- 4) \\cdot R_1$ on $A?$"] [17592186059580 :question/worked-solution "The operation $R_2:=R_2 + (-4) R_1$ means that we need to add $-4$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nCarrying out this row operation, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4+(-4)(1) & 2+(-4)(2) & -1+(-4)(3) \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -13 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059961 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ on $M?$"] [17592186059961 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3+(3)(-1) & -1+(3)(2) & 9+(3)(4)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186056126 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186056127 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186056128 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186056129 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186056130 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186386022 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186386023 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186386024 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186386025 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186386026 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186059962 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ on $A?$"] [17592186059962 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186235821 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186235931 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186236097 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186236593 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186237077 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186237897 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ on $A?$"] [17592186237897 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186235871 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186236128 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186237011 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186237219 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186237402 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186265796 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ on $A?$"] [17592186265796 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186263105 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186263515 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ \\frac{7}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 1 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186263800 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186264833 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186265210 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 18 & 27 & -9\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186265809 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186265809 :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $-2$ times the second row to the first row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0+(-2)(5) & 4+(-2)(2) & 7+(-2)(1) \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1+(1)(5) & 3+(1)(2) & 0+(1)(1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186264003 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186264101 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 8 & -9 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186264408 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186264445 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186264622 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186265810 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186265810 :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the third row to the first row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $5$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1+(3)(2) & 2+(3)(0) & 1+(3)(-1) \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -9+(5)(2) & 0+(5)(0) & -4+(5)(-1) \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186263030 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186263760 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -19 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186264465 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186264654 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186264760 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186287981 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1}$ on $X?$"] [17592186287981 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3+(-3)(1) & -1+(-3)(2) & 1+(-3)(1) \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186285663 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186285790 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186285902 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186286397 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186287007 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186386014 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $B?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186386014 :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $4$ times the first row to the second row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4+(4)(1) & 12+(4)(3) & 3+(4)(6) \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ -1+1 & 2+3 & 4+6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186386016 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186386017 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 21 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186386018 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186386019 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186386020 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186388062 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186388062 :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the second row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1+(3)(9) & -3+(3)(6) & -2+(3)(-7) \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28 & 15 & -23 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28+(-1)(-2) & 15+(-1)(4) & -23+(-1)(-3) \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 30 & 11 & -20 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186388064 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ -14 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186388065 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 30 & 11 & -20 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186388066 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28 & 15 & -23 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186388067 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ -5 & 9 & -11 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186388068 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 26 & 19 & -26 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186059581 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n![](images/82/82729e1d34174d58f01547b58aa63db28ec68a4e1964ef5cd127a2167ed4a722.png) \n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ on $A?$"] [17592186059581 :question/worked-solution "The operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059956 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ on $M?$"] [17592186059956 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5+(-1)(5) & -1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(-1) & 1+(-1)(1) \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186236231 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186236337 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186236920 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186237177 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186237275 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186059963 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A$, given by\n$A = \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]$.\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{1}:=2R_{1}$ on $A$?"] [17592186056138 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 10 \\\\ 8 & 12 & 14\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186056139 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 12 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 24 & 28\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186056140 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186056141 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\