ed to swap the first and third rows.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4+(-1)(-1) & 4+(-1)(9) & 6+(-1)(-2) & 7+(-1)(6) \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186263962 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186264202 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186264355 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -10 & 9 & -7 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186264672 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186264841 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186341857 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $M?$"] [17592186341857 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1+(-1)(1) & -1+(-1)(0) & 1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(3)\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186339758 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186339797 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186340679 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186340698 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186341011 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186341863 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $U,$ given by\n\n$$\nU=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $U?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186341863 :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}$ means that we need to multiply the second row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0+0 & -1+1 & -3+0 & 4+3\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186339173 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 10\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186339802 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 10\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186339971 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186340069 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 10\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186340394 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -7\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186388069 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ on $A?$"] [17592186388069 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $-\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $-\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{3}:=(-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 6 & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot (-3) & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 9 & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 0\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186388071 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & -\\frac{8}{3} & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186388072 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186388073 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186388074 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186388075 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393222 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ on $T?$"] [17592186393222 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2+(2)(1) & -2+(2)(3) & 1+(2)(2)\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186393224 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393225 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -4\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393226 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -5\\end{array}\\right]"] [1759218639