* The system has a unique solution"] [17592186115752 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 13 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 13 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 75\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -150\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-150,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."] [17592186438106 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438107 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438108 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438109 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438110 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438111 :answer/value "true"] [17592186115832 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+z &=0 \\\\ -4x+6y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n\n- **II.** The system has no solution\n\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent"] [17592186115832 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."] [17592186438296 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438297 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438298 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438299 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438300 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438301 :answer/value "true"] [17592186266113 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=-1 \\\\ 2x+8y &=-2 \\\\ -3x-12y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n\n- **III.** The system has a unique solution"] [17592186266113 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we can find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."] [17592186437878 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437879 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437880 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437881 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437882 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437883 :answer/value "true"] [17592186266114 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z &=3 \\\\ -3x+3y-3z &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system has a unique solution\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent"] [17592186266114 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 19\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=19,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."] [17592186437902 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437903 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437904 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437905 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437906 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437907 :answer/value "true"] [17592186266115 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=2 \\\\ -3x-4y &=3 \\\\ 2x-4y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system has a unique solution\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [17592186266115 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-5,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."] [17592186437908 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437909 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437910 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437911 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437912 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437913 :answer/value "true"] [17592186344956 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y+3z &=0 \\\\ x+3y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system has no solution\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent"] [17592186344956 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & \\frac{3}{2} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means that  we can find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."] [17592186438520 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438521 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438522 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438523 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438524 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438525 :answer/value "true"] [17592186344957 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y &=-1 \\\\ x-2y &=1 \\\\ -x-5y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system has no solution\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent"] [17592186344957 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=1 \\\\ 7y &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-\\frac{3}{7}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-\\frac{3}{7})=1\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\n \nSo, we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."] [17592186438526 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438527 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438528 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438529 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438530 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438531 :answer/value "true"] [17592186363108 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+z &=2 \\\\ -2x+7y+2z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system has no solution\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent"] [17592186363108 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."] [17592186437872 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437873 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437874 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437875 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437876 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437877 :answer/value "true"] [17592186364365 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=8 \\\\ x+y &=-2 \\\\ x+\\frac{1}{2}y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system has no solution\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent"] [17592186364365 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=-2 \\\\ -y &=14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-14.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-14)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=12.\n$$\n\n \nSo,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent.   \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."] [17592186438532 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438533 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438534 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438535 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438536 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438537 :answer/value "true"] [17592186400632 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-6y-2z &=4 \\\\ 3x-9y-3z &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system has no solution\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent"] [17592186400632 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -6 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -6 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x,$ and we have two free variables, $y$ and $z.$ That means we can find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."] [17592186437884 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437885 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437886 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437887 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437888 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437889 :answer/value "true"] [17592186400639 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 3x+7y &=1 \\\\ -2x-4y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system has no solution\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent"] [17592186400639 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ y &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=4$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=-9.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."] [17592186437890 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437891 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437892 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437893 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437894 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437895 :answer/value "true"] [17592186400646 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-3y &=6 \\\\ -2x+y &=-3 \\\\ 4x-4y &=8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system has no solution"] [17592186400646 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=2 \\\\ y &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=-1$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=1.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."] [17592186437896 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437897 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437898 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437899 :answer/value "true"] [17592186437900 :answer/value "false"] [17592186437901 :answer/value "true"] [17592186402763 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 3x+y &=3 \\\\ -2x+y &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system has a unique solution\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [17592186402763 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=2,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."] [17592186438290 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438291 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438292 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438293 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438294 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438295 :answer/value "true"] [17592186403787 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=-1 \\\\ 2x-4y &=3 \\\\ x+y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n\n- **II.** The system has a unique solution\n\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [17592186403787 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we will first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=\\frac{9}{2},$ and it has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."] [17592186438514 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438515 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438516 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438517 :answer/value "true"] [17592186438518 :answer/value "false"] [17592186438519 :answer/value "true"] [17592186492840 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-1 \\\\ 2x-7y &=0 \\\\ -4x+15y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\n\nII. The system has no solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent dependent"] [17592186492840 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-1 \\\\ y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=2$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=7.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."] [17592186492400 :answer/value "II and III only"] [17592186492502 :answer/value "III only"] [17592186492536 :answer/value "I and II only"] [17592186492568 :answer/value "I only"] [17592186492701 :answer/value "II only"] [17592186523101 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=0 \\\\ x+4y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [17592186523101 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."] [17592186523118 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523127 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523092 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523124 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523103 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523137 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523112 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-2z &=-4 \\\\ x+3y &=-8 \\\\ x+y-4z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [17592186523112 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."] [17592186523108 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523135 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523157 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523159 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523169 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523176 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523119 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-5 \\\\ -2x+6y &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [17592186523119 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. Here there is one free variable, $y$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."] [17592186523151 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523153 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523102 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523140 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523162 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523191 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523120 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=0 \\\\ -2x-y-7z &=-2 \\\\ 2x+11z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent"] [17592186523120 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 11 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 11 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 11 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 7 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."] [17592186523117 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523129 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523121 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523188 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523143 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523187 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523134 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=5 \\\\ x+2y+2z &=7 \\\\ x+3y+5z &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [17592186523134 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."] [17592186523107 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523182 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523130 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523133 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523123 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523150 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523146 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z &=1 \\\\ 2x+5y &=7 \\\\ -2x-3y+5z &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent"] [17592186523146 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."] [17592186523122 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523186 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523158 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523164 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523095 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523132 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523149 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=1 \\\\ 2x+4y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent"] [17592186523149 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."] [17592186523163 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523167 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523100 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523142 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523098 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523139 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523165 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=4 \\\\ -x &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [17592186523165 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."] [17592186523126 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523147 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523125 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523189 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523105 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523111 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523181 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-3z &=5 \\\\ 2x-5y-9z &=10 \\\\ 2x-5y-9z &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent"] [17592186523181 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. Here there is one free variable, $z$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."] [17592186523152 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523170 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523166 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523178 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523141 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523171 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523190 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-3 \\\\ -2x-4y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [17592186523190 :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."] [17592186523136 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523183 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523096 :answer/value "false"] [17592186523116 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523099 :answer/value "true"] [17592186523174 :answer/value "false"] [17592186163179 :tutorial/content "We can do the same trick using the **elementary column operations** instead of row operations.\n\nThere are three types of elementary *column* operations, which are entirely analogous to the corresponding row operations:\n\n- Switching any two columns: \n\n$$\nC_i \\leftrightarrow C_j\n$$\n\n- Multiplying (each element of) a column by a non-zero number: \n\n$$\nC_i := k C_i,\\qquad k \\neq 0\n$$\n\n- Adding a multiple of one column to another column: \n\n$$\nC_j := C_j+k C_i,\\qquad j \\neq i\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** \n\n- Unlike elementary row operations, elementary *column* operations change the solutions of a system of linear equations. This is because column operations alter the coefficients associated with each variable across the system, changing the equations.\n\n- The exception is swapping two columns - this doesn't alter the solutions *provided that* we swap the corresponding variables in the solution vector. For example, if we swap the first and second columns, we must treat the second variable as the first and vice versa. The solution set remains unchanged because the relationships between the variables and their coefficients are preserved."] [17592186163214 :tutorial/content "When studying linear algebra, it is common to use elementary row operations to reduce a matrix $A$ to another matrix $B$ such that $B$ contains many zeros. \n\nTo illustrate, let's consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the entry $a_{11}$ located in the top left-hand corner. We can reduce *all* of the entries *below* it using elementary row operations.\n\nFirst, we subtract $3$ times the first row from the second row.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A= & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}: &={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10 \\\\ -5 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we add $5$ times the first row to the third row.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10 \\\\ -5 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}: &={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -14\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we're done! We have successfully performed elementary row operations to reduce all of the entries below $a_{11}$ to zero."] [17592186161757 :question/problem "![](images/1d/1d7b89b6790ed713a8885b5124d988cda34cccff589ceaef9d556708bc21233f.png)\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary row operations \n\n- $R_1 := \\ldots$\n\n- $R_3:=R_3-3R_2$\n\n- $R_4:= \\ldots$\n\neach of the form $R_i:=R_i+kR_2,$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary row operations?"] [17592186161757 :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries above and below $a_{22}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}$ equal to ${\\color{red}0}.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}: &={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}: &={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}: &={R}_{4}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\qquad$ $R_1 := R_1 - 2R_2\\quad$ and $\\quad R_4:=R_4+2R_2.$"] [17592186162554 :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}13 & 0 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 19 & 2 \\\\ 25 & 0 & 19 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary row operations \n\n- ${R}_{1}:=…$\n- ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2}$\n- ${R}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary row operations?"] [17592186162554 :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries above and below ${a}_{22}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}: &={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}13 & 0 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}: &={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}13 & 0 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 19 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}: &={R}_{4}+5{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}13 & 0 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 19 & 2 \\\\ 25 & 0 & 19 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+5{R}_{2}.$"] [17592186326991 :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-4{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-5{R}_{2}$"] [17592186327324 :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-5{R}_{2}$"] [17592186327958 :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+5{R}_{2}$"] [17592186328739 :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+4{R}_{2}$"] [17592186329114 :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-4{R}_{2}$"] [17592186162571 :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 10 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 8 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -14 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary row operations \n\n- ${R}_{2}:=…$\n- ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$\n- ${R}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary row operations?"] [17592186162571 :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries below ${a}_{11}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 10 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 8 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}: &={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 8 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}: &={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}: &={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -14 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}.$"] [17592186412015 :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}$"] [17592186412016 :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{