}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{1}.$"] [17592186263338 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{1}$"] [17592186264476 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+4{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{1}$"] [17592186264498 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{1}$"] [17592186264521 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-4{C}_{1}$"] [17592186264888 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-4{C}_{1}$"] [17592186265939 :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 15 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?"] [17592186265939 :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 15 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}: &={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}: &={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}.$"] [17592186263193 :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}$"] [17592186263200 :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}$"] [17592186263430 :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-5{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{