 to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}: &={C}_{2}-{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}: &={C}_{3}-9{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-9{C}_{1}.$"] [17592186354786 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+9{C}_{1}$"] [17592186355022 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-3{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-3{C}_{1}$"] [17592186355359 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-9{C}_{1}$"] [17592186356251 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-9{C}_{1}$"] [17592186356474 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-9{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}$"] [17592186394847 :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -7 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -11 & -7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?"] [17592186394847 :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left of ${a}_{13}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -7 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}: &={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -11 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}: &={C}_{2}-{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -11 & -7 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{3}.$"] [17592186394849 :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{3}$"] [17592186394850 :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{3}$"] [17592186394851 :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{3}$"] [17592186394852 :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{3}$"] [17592186394853 :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-6{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{3}$"] [17592186412026 :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?"] [17592186412026 :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of ${a}_{31}=3$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}: &={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}: &={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}.$"] [17592186412014 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{1}$"] [17592186412017 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+3{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+2{C}_{1}$"] [17592186412018 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}$"] [17592186412020 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-2{C}_{1}$"] [17592186412021 :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}$"] [17592186097840 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to solve the following system of linear equations:\n![](images/b6/b6441688c486562e704a29317847ba53ca5130ff6e35c9d4effdea5ede005d3f.svg)\nThe augmented matrix for this system can be written as \n![](images/b4/b45896f12f8195fcb211411a9a2dcd230cee288822e2d37f2b364f6c1c831c6d.svg)\n\nNotice that the matrix is in *row echelon form* (or REF). Whenever the augmented matrix is in row echelon form, we can solve the system using a method called **back substitution**.\n\nBack substitution involves\n\n- starting with the lowest equation (which is already solved for one variable),\n\n- substituting the result into the next-lowest equation to find the solution for another variable, and\n\n- continuing to substitute the result into the next-lowest equation until the values of all the variables have been found.\n\nHere, the third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny -(3) = 2 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = 5.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $y=5$ and $z=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx + 2(5) + (3) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx = -12.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-12,$ $y=5,$ and $z=3.$ We can write it in vector form, as follows:\n\n![](images/8b/8bbbabd0167fc73c58c095fb11ed5efb2c2dca63ee90e95717e26f30f0f170e9.svg)\n\n**Note:** The values $x=-12,$ $y=5,$ and $z=3$ together form *one* solution. We say that this system has *one* solution, *not* three solutions. A system with three solutions would have three different solution vectors, whereas here, we only have *one* solution vector."] [17592186096456 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n![](images/31/31969ec4b2fc35f5175b3cfd114b79b5b9ba608241aa1d9c45f1a7c37484fd21.svg)"] [17592186096456 :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(2)=2 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = 2-2 = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $z=2$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(2)=3\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx = 3-2 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 1,$ $y=0,$ and $z = 2.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 1,0,2 \\rangle.$"] [17592186097178 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186097178 :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-(2)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}+2=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(\\frac{5}{2})-(2)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3+2-\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{2}$, ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{5}{2},2⟩.$"] [17592186285754 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5}{2},1,\\frac{5}{2}⟩"] [17592186285832 :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2},2⟩"] [17592186286005 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2},2⟩"] [17592186286651 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2},2,-\\frac{3}{2}⟩"] [17592186286872 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{5}{2},2⟩"] [17592186097182 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1} + 3x_{2} - 2x_{3} &=-5 \\\\ x_{2} - x_{3} &=\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ x_{3} &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.$"] [17592186095066 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{13}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186095067 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186095068 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186095069 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{17}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186095070 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186237857 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y+z &=1 \\\\ z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186237857 :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that  $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\ny+2=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-2=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=2$ and $y=-1$into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-1)+(2)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}-2+1=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, $y=-1$, and $z=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩.$"] [17592186235851 :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{3}{2},1,2⟩"] [17592186236461 :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{3}{2},-1,2⟩"] [17592186236998 :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩"] [17592186237293 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{2},1,2⟩"] [17592186237311 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩"] [17592186237858 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=-1 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186237858 :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=3.$ Substitute this into the second equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-(3)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1+3=2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(2)+(3)=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1-3+2=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=0$,  ${x}_{2}=2$, and ${x}_{3}=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,2,3⟩.$"] [17592186236236 :answer/value "⟨1,-3,2⟩"] [17592186236413 :answer/value "⟨0,2,3⟩"] [17592186236525 :answer/value "⟨1,-3,0⟩"] [17592186237405 :answer/value "⟨1,3,2⟩"] [17592186237432 :answer/value "⟨0,3,-2⟩"] [17592186237860 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y-z &=4 \\\\ y+2z &=2 \\\\ z &=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186237860 :question/worked-solution "he third equation states that  $z=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+2(\\frac{1}{2})=2\\,⟹\\,y=2-1=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(1)-(\\frac{1}{2})=4\\,⟹\\,x=4+1+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{11}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{11}{2}$,  $y=1$, and $z=\\frac{1}{2}.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨\\frac{11}{2},1,\\frac{1}{2}⟩.$"] [17592186236242 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{11}{2},1,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] [17592186236315 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{9}{2},1,2⟩"] [17592186236415 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{9}{2},2,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] [17592186236596 :answer/value "⟨1,\\frac{9}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] [17592186237088 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩"] [17592186237861 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=9 \\\\ {x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186237861 :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that  ${x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-3(\\frac{1}{3})=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=2+1=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(3)+3(\\frac{1}{3})=9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=9+3-1=11.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=11$, ${x}_{2}=3$, and ${x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{3}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨11,3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩.$"] [17592186235859 :answer/value "⟨12,-3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] [17592186236299 :answer/value "⟨9,-3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] [17592186236494 :answer/value "⟨11,3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] [17592186236922 :answer/value "⟨9,2,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] [17592186237139 :answer/value "⟨11,3,3⟩"] [17592186237863 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y-z &=3 \\\\ y-z &=2 \\\\ z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186237863 :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that $z=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-(1)=2\\,⟹\\,y=2+1=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=1$ and $y=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(3)-(1)=3\\,⟹\\,x=3+4=7.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=7$,  $y=3$,  and $z=1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨7,3,1⟩.$"] [17592186236034 :answer/value "⟨6,2,1⟩"] [17592186236234 :answer/value "⟨5,3,-1⟩"] [17592186236757 :answer/value "⟨7,3,1⟩"] [17592186236868 :answer/value "⟨5,2,0⟩"] [17592186236985 :answer/value "⟨7,-2,-1⟩"] [17592186265729 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186265729 :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-1)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(\\frac{1}{2})+(-1)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2+1+1=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=4$, ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}$, and ${x}_{3}=-1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨4,\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩.$"] [17592186263657 :answer/value "⟨4,\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩"] [17592186263724 :answer/value "⟨2,\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩"] [17592186263896 :answer/value "⟨2,-\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩"] [17592186264544 :answer/value "⟨4,-\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩"] [17592186265173 :answer/value "⟨0,-\\frac{3}{2},-1⟩"] [17592186265730 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-z &=2 \\\\ y-z &=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186265730 :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-3=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}+3=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $y=\\frac{7}{2}$ and $z=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+\\frac{7}{2}-3=2\\,⟹\\,x=2-\\frac{7}{2}+3=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{3}{2}$, $y=\\frac{7}{2}$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$"] [17592186263173 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186263191 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186263486 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186263818 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186264993 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186265731 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186265731 :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-2)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=2+2=4.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=4$ and ${x}_{3}=-2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-4-(-2)=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=4+4-2=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=6$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=-2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨6,4,-2⟩.$"] [17592186263777 :answer/value "⟨0,-4,-2⟩"] [17592186264879 :answer/value "⟨6,-4,-2⟩"] [17592186264985 :answer/value "⟨6,4,-2⟩"] [17592186265045 :answer/value "⟨6,0,-2⟩"] [17592186265251 :answer/value "⟨2,0,-2⟩"] [17592186265732 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-6{x}_{3} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186265732 :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-6(-\\frac{1}{3})=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3-2=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+1-(-\\frac{1}{3})=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2-1-\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{2}{3}$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.$"] [17592186263370 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186263433 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ -1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186263502 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186263517 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186263585 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186413953 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y-z &=4 \\\\ y+z &=2 \\\\ z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186413953 :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get  \n\n$$\ny+(3)=2\\,⟹\\,y=2-3=-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(-1)-(3)=4\\,⟹\\,x=4-1+3=6.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=6$, $y=-1$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$"] [17592186413947 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186413948 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186413949 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186413950 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186413951 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186096457 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n![](images/c3/c33de841c5e1997fba4e26afca5750a0125fa1fcd98bd98993feadaab063c1c9.svg)"] [17592186096457 :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n![](images/48/484ee8f84ffa8585eb318ce50ab707ddcc13ba695d32100f85850ba5f408725d.svg)\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-5=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13,$ $x_2=-7,$ and $x_3 = 5.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle.$"] [17592186096925 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186096925 :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=1 \\\\ y+z &=1 \\\\ z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(1)=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=1$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(1)=1\\,⟹\\,x=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=0$, and $z=1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,0,1⟩.$"] [17592186235965 :answer/value "⟨0,1,1⟩"] [17592186236139 :answer/value "⟨0,1,0⟩"] [17592186236938 :answer/value "⟨1,1,1⟩"] [17592186237040 :answer/value "⟨1,0,1⟩"] [17592186237135 :answer/value "⟨0,0,1⟩"] [17592186097179 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186097179 :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say,  ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=5 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(2)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(-2)+4(2)=5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=5-6-8=-9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=-9$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-9,-2,2⟩.$"] [17592186285566 :answer/value "⟨1,-8,-2⟩"] [17592186285718 :answer/value "⟨-9,-2,2⟩"] [17592186286079 :answer/value "⟨8,1,2⟩"] [17592186286792 :answer/value "⟨-3,-1,2⟩"] [17592186287056 :answer/value "⟨3,0,2⟩"] [17592186265733 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186265733 :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say,  ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}+\\frac{{x}_{3}}{3} &=-1 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+\\frac{2}{3}=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1-\\frac{2}{3}=-\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{3}$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3(-\\frac{5}{3})+(2)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2+5-2=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=5$, ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{3}$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨5,-\\frac{5}{3},2⟩.$"] [17592186263120 :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{3},2⟩"] [17592186263329 :answer/value "⟨1,\\frac{1}{3},2⟩"] [17592186263466 :answer/value "⟨3,-\\frac{5}{3},2⟩"] [17592186264010 :answer/value "⟨5,-\\frac{5}{3},2⟩"] [17592186265207 :answer/value "⟨5,-\\frac{1}{3},2⟩"] [17592186265734 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186265734 :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+3z &=-2 \\\\ y+4z &=0 \\\\ z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+4(3)=0\\,⟹\\,y=-12.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-12$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-12)+3(3)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-2+12-9=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1$, $y=-12$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨1,-12,3⟩.$"] [17592186263303 :answer/value "⟨-1,-12,3⟩"] [17592186263748 :answer/value "⟨-22,-12,3⟩"] [17592186263895 :answer/value "⟨-22,12,3⟩"] [