186264514 :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186264936 :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186323937 :question/problem "Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=3 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3} &=-10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form."] [17592186323937 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -11 & -10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -11 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -11 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186321671 :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186321897 :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186322005 :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186322094 :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186322181 :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186342119 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] [17592186342119 :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+y-2z &=-5 \\\\ 0x+2y-2z &=-3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=-5,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution."] [17592186340380 :answer/value "No solution"] [17592186340812 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186340864 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186340963 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186341148 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186342120 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 & 18\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] [17592186342120 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 & 18\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -12 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 & 18\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -12 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 34\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y-6z &=8 \\\\ 0x-y-12z &=16 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=34\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=34,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution."] [17592186339464 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1-3y \\\\ 4-z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186340170 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8+6z \\\\ -4-3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186340172 :answer/value "No solution"] [17592186340821 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4-3z \\\\ 8+6z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186341282 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8-2y+6z \\\\ -4-3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186342121 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -12 & 14 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -19 & 15\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] [17592186342121 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -12 & 14 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -19 & 15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -19 & 15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y-5z &=6 \\\\ 0x+y+3z &=-4 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=-9,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution."] [17592186339175 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6+3y-5z \\\\ -4-2z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186339740 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12-2y \\\\ 4-3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186340471 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6-3y+5z \\\\ -4-3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186340622 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2-2y-6z \\\\ 4z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186340852 :answer/value "No solution"] [17592186342122 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -12 & -6 & 16 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2 & 5 & 12 \\\\ 2 & -20 & -4 & 25\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] [17592186342122 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -12 & -6 & 16 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2 & 5 & 12 \\\\ 2 & -20 & -4 & 25\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -12 & -6 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -20 & -4 & 25\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -12 & -6 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -12 & -6 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -12 & -6 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-12y-6z &=16 \\\\ 0x+y+2z &=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=-11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=-11,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution."] [17592186340025 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16+12y-6z \\\\ 1-2z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186340077 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12y-6z \\\\ 1-2z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186340865 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12-2y-6z \\\\ 4-z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186341134 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16+6z \\\\ 12-2z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186341153 :answer/value "No solution"] [17592186395978 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] [17592186395978 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=2 \\\\ 0x+y-3z &=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution."] [17592186395980 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2-y-z \\\\ 4-z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186395981 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3y \\\\ y \\\\ 4y-1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186395982 :answer/value "No solution"] [17592186395983 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1-3y \\\\ y \\\\ 2+y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186395984 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2-y-z \\\\ 1+z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186403731 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] [17592186403731 :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y+2z &=1 \\\\ 0x-2y+4z &=3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=10,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution."] [17592186403733 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186403734 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186403735 :answer/value "No solution"] [17592186403736 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [17592186403737 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]]